Protocol reference audited against RustDesk 1.5.3 (95cca3f661f635b3cc85c04935fe8d96d8f432ef),
hbb_common fae47e024dd83cef6aaecde0aa7d11731df11649, the submodule pinned by that release.
Relative to 1.5.0, message.proto adds optional trusted-device v2 and OS-login
fields; rendezvous.proto adds the USB permission bit. Existing field numbers,
KX, signed rendezvous and WebRTC framing are unchanged. The partial endpoint
does not advertise trusted-device v2, handle OS-login messages or implement
remote-USB control; it continues to authenticate using the password challenge.
The original 1.5.0 KX wire fixtures round-trip unchanged through the 1.5.3 schema.
This is a partial protocol endpoint derived via OneKVM, not a complete RustDesk client fork.
RustDesk 1.5.0 KX v1, signed rendezvous parameters, DTLS identity binding,
WebRTC data-channel framing and temporary-password rotation are adapted from
the pinned RustDesk/hbb_common commits. The application bridge uses Pion v4.2.22;
its source and standalone tests are included under app-webrtc in the source archive.
